  "worked_solution": "The range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061x$ is given by\n\n$$\n0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nNote that the angle $\\theta $ spans the first and second quadrants.\n\nSince $-\\frac{1}{2}$ is negative, our answer is an angle that lies in the second quadrant, where cosine is negative.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14035417/assets/dbf36192ac332dc49ed75278838e989a37ac7d888311be1b8b059a7b59667aa6.png)\n\nFrom the values in the second quadrant, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061(-\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\n$$",
